<title>USA: Kent State University, Ohio, $37 mln repriced.</title>
<headline>Kent State University, Ohio, $37 mln repriced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Nuveen &amp; Co said that it repriced and restructured on Wednesday and then received the award on a $37.28 million Kent State University, Ohio, general receipts bond issue, Series 1996, with a top yield of 5.80 percent in 2028.</p>
<p>The top yield was raised to 5.80 percent from 5.75 percent in 2028 and to 5.70 percent from 5.65 percent in 2017.</p>
<p>And a 2013 maturity was added and amounts in various maturities were adjusted.</p>
<p>The bonds are book entry and MBIA insured.</p>
<p>The bonds are rated Aaa by Moody's Investors Service and AAA by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The bonds are dated 10/15/1996 and due 5/1.</p>
<p>The first coupon is 5/1/1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected 11/12/1996 and the award is expected 10/30/1996.</p>
<p>The bonds are callable 11/1/2006 at 102.00 and declining to par 11/1/2008 at 100.00.</p>
